%% ---------------------------------------------------------------- B
\appx{B}{Penetration Test: Scope, Commands and Results}
\textbf{Scope and isolation.} Target: the group's own fictional application, run as a separate disposable Docker stack (own project, network, volume, keys and passwords) on localhost only (HTTP 9180, HTTPS 9543 for the first campaign; the live lab on 8443 for the retest). Excluded: university production systems, public websites, third-party databases, real accounts, password lists, denial-of-service load, credential exfiltration. Database tests used the restricted \code{grants_app} account as the \emph{attack} identity; administrative access only prepared the lab and collected evidence. Tools: \code{curl}, \code{openssl}, \code{bc}, \code{psql}, \code{docker}, and the harnesses in \code{scripts/pentest/}. The \code{curl} listings below are representative equivalents of what the scripts send; the raw script output is the authority for every number.
\begin{lstlisting}[language=bash]
python3 scripts/pentest/prepare-lab.py                 # copy sources (no secrets) to a disposable lab
scripts/pentest.sh                                     # black-box checks (curl/openssl only)
python3 scripts/pentest/http-deep.py                   # first campaign: TLS-verified HTTP, timing, throttling
PENTEST_LAB=1 DB_NAME=grants_test php scripts/pentest/deep-db.php    # restricted SQL probes
\end{lstlisting}

\subsubsection*{B.1 Reconnaissance, transport and exposure}
\begin{lstlisting}[language=bash]
for p in /.git/config /.env /config/config.php /secrets/web.env /backups/ /database/02_schema.sql /src/App.php \
         /logs/app-error.log /server-status /assets/ /phpinfo.php /index.php~; do
  printf '%s -> ' "$p"; curl -ks -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' "https://localhost:8443$p"; done
curl -ks --path-as-is -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' "https://localhost:8443/assets/%2e%2e/%2e%2e/secrets/web.env"
for m in TRACE PUT DELETE OPTIONS PATCH; do curl -ks -X $m -o /dev/null -w "$m %{http_code}\n" https://localhost:8443/proposals; done
openssl s_client -connect localhost:8443 -tls1_1 </dev/null 2>&1 | grep -i "alert\|error"
\end{lstlisting}
All files returned 400/403/404 without content; traversal 400; unusual methods 404/405; SSLv3, TLS 1.0 and 1.1 refused; plain HTTP answers 301 to HTTPS; ports 5432, 80, 443 are not reachable on the host (80 and 443 are published only on 127.0.0.1:8080/8443). \resisted{RESISTED}. A 404 on selected paths does not prove the whole filesystem is inaccessible.

\subsubsection*{B.2 Authentication, session and CSRF}
\begin{lstlisting}[language=bash]
T=$(curl -ks -c jar https://localhost:8443/login | grep -o 'name="_csrf" value="[^"]*"' | cut -d'"' -f4)
curl -ks -b jar -c jar -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' --data-urlencode "_csrf=$T" \
     --data-urlencode "email=' OR '1'='1' --" --data-urlencode "password=x" https://localhost:8443/login      # -> 401
curl -ks -b victim -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' -d "title=x" https://localhost:8443/proposals            # no token -> 400
curl -ks -b victim -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' https://localhost:8443/logout                            # GET -> 404
\end{lstlisting}
SQL injection and array-parameter logins return 401 with identical error text for unknown account and wrong password; anonymous access to protected routes returns 303; a planted session id is replaced at login (no fixation); the cookie is HttpOnly, Secure and \code{\_\_Host-} prefixed; a copied cookie is rejected after logout; forged POSTs return 400 and create no data. \resisted{RESISTED}.

\subsubsection*{B.3 Authorization, tampering and injection}
Attackers: researcher \code{youssef.benali} and reviewer \code{karim.ouazzani}. Each denial is read after a positive control (the owner opens the same resource with 200).
\begin{center}\scriptsize
\begin{tabularx}{\linewidth}{@{}YL{2.8cm}L{2.2cm}@{}}\toprule\textbf{Attack}&\textbf{Observed}&\textbf{Verdict}\\\midrule
Researcher reads / edits / submits another's proposal or draft & 404 & \resisted{RESISTED}\\
Researcher deletes another's draft & 403 & \resisted{RESISTED}\\
Researcher requests \code{/officer}, \code{/officer/calls}, \code{/audit}, \code{/reviews}, \code{/reviews/N}; records a decision; assigns a reviewer; creates a call & 403 each & \resisted{RESISTED}\\
Reviewer opens or overwrites a colleague's review; records a decision & 404 / 403; score unchanged & \resisted{RESISTED}\\
Mass assignment (\code{status}, \code{owner\_id}, \code{currency} in the body) & ignored; row stays draft, own owner, MAD & \resisted{RESISTED}\\
Amounts \code{-500}, \code{0}, \code{1e9}, \code{0x10}, \code{10;DROP}, \code{99999999999999999999}, \code{1.999}, \code{NaN}; path id \code{1\%20OR\%201=1} & 422 each; 404 & \resisted{RESISTED}\\
Seven SQL payloads in the search box and six in the audit filters (UNION, error-based, \code{pg\_sleep}, wildcards) & no foreign row, no error, no delay & \resisted{RESISTED}\\
Stored and reflected script payloads; \code{Host} header reflection & escaped; not reflected & \resisted{RESISTED}\\
Superuser, guessed password, no-TLS and backup account connections from the web container to the database & rejected by \code{pg\_hba} or authentication (5 of 5) & \resisted{RESISTED}\\
\bottomrule\end{tabularx}\end{center}

\subsubsection*{B.4 Brute force, lockout and timing (first campaign and retest)}
\begin{lstlisting}[language=bash]
for i in 1 2 3 4 5 6; do   # failed anonymous logins on a KNOWN account, then the CORRECT password
  curl -ks -b j -c j -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' --data-urlencode "_csrf=$T" \
    --data-urlencode "email=omar.chraibi@uni.example" --data-urlencode "password=wrong$i" https://localhost:8443/login; done
\end{lstlisting}
\begin{center}\small
\begin{tabularx}{\linewidth}{@{}L{3.0cm}YY@{}}\toprule & \textbf{11 November (before)} & \textbf{17 November (after)}\\\midrule
F02 five failures, known account & 401 x5; account lock in database; correct password also 401 & 401 x5; no account-wide lock; attacker address locked, owner's other address open\\
F03 timing, 20 samples per class & unknown 251.756, unlocked 254.366, \textbf{locked 27.996} ms (medians) & 151.628 / 147.796 / 148.652 ms\\
F04 30 attempts, 30 accounts & 30 of 30 processed (all 401) in 7.69 s & 20 processed (401), 10 refused (429), \code{Retry-After: 600}\\
\bottomrule\end{tabularx}\end{center}
Method for the timing samples: randomized order with a fixed seed, valid CSRF token, every response must be 401 (a redirect or CSRF rejection stops the run instead of being counted as a fast failure), the CSRF fetch is excluded from the duration, and the operator clears throttle state between samples exactly as the first campaign reset its lock counter.

\subsubsection*{B.5 Database-level probes (attacker holds the runtime credential)}
\begin{lstlisting}[language=SQLx,caption={F01 probe, as grants\_app on grants\_test (first campaign: committed; retest: refused with 42501)}]
BEGIN;
-- first campaign: SELECT set_config('app.user_id', '<officer id>', true);   (a claim: now ignored)
SELECT set_config('app.actor', '<valid token>', true);   -- retest: the web process, which holds the key (proposal_id, outcome, awarded_amount, currency, decided_by)
VALUES (1, 'approved', 1.00, 'MAD', <officer id>);      -- before: COMMIT succeeded, balance and status unchanged
COMMIT;
\end{lstlisting}
In the first campaign the committed 1.00 award left the balance at 600\,000.00 and the proposal \emph{under review} (invariant difference $-1.00$). In the retest the same statement, a lone balance update and a call to \code{record_decision()} by a researcher all fail with SQLSTATE 42501, the single permitted door awards 1.00 and the invariant difference is 0.00. The same script now also models an attacker who holds \emph{only} the database password: a claimed officer sees 0 proposals (DB03, was 18) and a direct INSERT into \code{audit\_events} or a call to \code{audit\_append()} without a token is refused with 42501 (DB05).

%% ---------------------------------------------------------------- C
\appx{C}{Selected Source Excerpts (Remediation Release)}
\begin{lstlisting}[language=PHP,caption={src/Auth/Authenticator.php: one hashing cost on every failed path (F03) and counting per address (F02, F04)}]
if ($this->gate(null) === 'ip_throttled') { throw new LoginThrottled($this->config['ip_window_minutes'] * 60); }   // cheap refusal
$stmt = $pdo->prepare('SELECT * FROM auth_find_credentials(?)'); $stmt->execute([$email]); $cred = $stmt->fetch();
if ($cred === false)            { password_verify($password, self::DUMMY_HASH); $this->fail(null, null, 'unknown_account'); return null; }
if (!$cred['is_active'])        { password_verify($password, self::DUMMY_HASH); $this->fail($user, $user->id, 'account_disabled'); return null; }
if ($this->gate($user->id) === 'pair_locked')
                                { password_verify($password, self::DUMMY_HASH); $this->fail($user, $user->id, 'account_locked', [...]); return null; }
if (!password_verify($password, $cred['password_hash'])) { $this->fail($user, $user->id, 'bad_password'); return null; }
\end{lstlisting}
\begin{lstlisting}[language=PHP,caption={src/Auth/Authenticator.php: after the password, officers and auditors owe a code (condensed)}]
$state = $this->mfaState($user);                                  // mfa_state(): needs a token for this very user
if ($state['enrolled'] || in_array($user->role, $this->config['mfa']['required_roles'], true)) {
    $this->session->regenerate();
    $this->session->set('mfa_pending', ['user_id' => $user->id, 'at' => time(), 'attempts' => 0]);   // not signed in yet
    return new MfaChallenge($user, $state['enrolled']);
}
...
$step = Totp::matchStep($secret, $input, $this->config['mfa']['window']);                // constant-time, +-1 step
if ($step === null) { return $this->mfaFail($user, 'bad_mfa'); }                          // counts like a wrong password
if ($this->config['mfa']['replay_protection'] && !$this->acceptStep($user, $step)) { return $this->mfaFail($user, 'mfa_replay'); }
return $this->finishLogin($user, 'totp');                                                 // new session id, audit with the method
\end{lstlisting}
\begin{lstlisting}[language=SQLx,caption={database/05\_remediation.sql: throttle functions (condensed); the runtime role has no privilege on the table}]
CREATE TABLE login_failures (id bigint GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY PRIMARY KEY, occurred_at timestamptz DEFAULT clock_timestamp(),
                             user_id bigint REFERENCES users (id), source_ip inet NOT NULL);
CREATE FUNCTION auth_login_gate(p_user_id bigint, p_ip inet, p_pair_max int, p_pair_minutes int, p_ip_max int, p_ip_minutes int)
  RETURNS text LANGUAGE sql STABLE SECURITY DEFINER SET search_path = grants, pg_temp AS $$ ... 'ip_throttled' | 'pair_locked' | NULL $$;
CREATE FUNCTION auth_record_failure(...) ...;   CREATE FUNCTION auth_clear_failures(p_user_id bigint, p_ip inet) ...;
ALTER TABLE users DROP COLUMN IF EXISTS failed_login_count;    -- the account-wide counter is gone
\end{lstlisting}
\begin{lstlisting}[language=PHP,caption={src/Grants/GrantWorkflow.php: the award is one database call (F01)}]
$stmt = $tx->prepare('SELECT decision_id, remaining FROM record_decision(?, ?, ?::numeric, ?, ?::uuid, ?::inet)');
try { $stmt->execute([$proposalId, $outcome, $amount, $rationale, $this->audit->correlationId(), $this->audit->ip()]); }
catch (\PDOException $e) {   // SQLSTATE GR001 = a business rule refused the award
    if (($e->errorInfo[0] ?? '') === 'GR001' && preg_match('/ERROR:\s+(\w+)\|([^\n]*)/', (string) $e->errorInfo[2], $m)) { throw new Denied($m[1], $m[2]); }
    throw $e; }
\end{lstlisting}
\begin{lstlisting}[language=PHP,caption={src/Security/FieldCipher.php: key id in the value; header authenticated}]
public function encrypt(string $plaintext, string $context): string {
    $id = $this->activeKeyId(); $nonce = random_bytes(SODIUM_CRYPTO_AEAD_XCHACHA20POLY1305_IETF_NPUBBYTES);
    $ct = sodium_crypto_aead_xchacha20poly1305_ietf_encrypt($plaintext, self::aad('v2', $id, $context), $nonce, $this->keys[$id]);
    return "v2:$id:" . base64_encode($nonce . $ct); }          // aad = "v2:<id>|reviews.comments:<row id>"
\end{lstlisting}

\subsubsection*{C.1 Repository layout}
\begin{center}\small
\begin{tabularx}{\linewidth}{@{}L{3.4cm}Y@{}}
\toprule\textbf{Location} & \textbf{Responsibility}\\\midrule
\code{public/} & The only directory Apache serves: front controller, CSS, JavaScript, icons\\
\code{src/Http}, \code{src/Auth} & Kernel and controllers; Argon2id authenticator, session, CSRF, role policy\\
\code{src/Grants} & \code{GrantWorkflow} (every write), \code{GrantQueries} (every read), exact money arithmetic\\
\code{src/Security}, \code{src/Audit}, \code{src/Mail} & \code{FieldCipher} keyring and \code{ActorToken}; audit through \code{audit\_append()} and the read-only reader; mail transports and the notifier\\
\code{database/} & Numbered SQL: \code{00} database access, \code{01} roles, \code{02} schema, \code{03} RLS, \code{05} remediation (F01--F04), \code{06} identity binding and audit, \code{07} review deadlines, \code{08} second factor, \code{09} notifications, \code{04} grants (applied last)\\
\code{scripts/} & Setup, tests, backup, restore, drills, evidence collection, key and custody tools, penetration-test harnesses\\
\code{docker/}, \code{compose.yaml} & Hardened images, \code{pg_hba.conf}, PostgreSQL settings, private network; the \code{notifier} service\\
\code{.github/} & CI workflow, retest checker, dependabot configuration\\
\bottomrule\end{tabularx}\end{center}


